TITLE:: MaxxedBeats
summary:: Entry point of the MaxxedBeats AI music assistant window
categories:: Assistant
related:: Guides/MaxxedBeats-Assistant, Classes/ChaosOsc

DESCRIPTION::
MaxxedBeats opens an in-SuperCollider assistant window. You describe music, the
provider and model you choose ("Choose your DJ") proposes a musical plan and
reviewable code changes to a project folder of code::.scd:: files, and approved
compositions are rendered offline to WAV with scsynth in a separate process.

Nothing is written, evaluated, or rendered without your explicit confirmation.
Prompts and the project files you select are sent to the provider you choose;
API usage may incur charges on your provider account. See
link::Guides/MaxxedBeats-Assistant:: for setup, privacy, cost, and
troubleshooting.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: gui
Open the assistant window, or bring it to the front if it is already open.

ARGUMENT:: services
Optional service port (an Event of functions). Omit it to use the installed
provider and workflow classes; see link::#*services::.

returns:: The window object.

METHOD:: current
returns:: The open window, or nil.

METHOD:: services
Build the service port that connects the window to the provider, credential
store, model catalog, usage meter, project, agent, renderer, and variation
classes.

ARGUMENT:: lookup
Optional function mapping a class name Symbol to a class; used by tests.

returns:: An Event of functions. Throws an MBError of kind code::\config:: when
part of MaxxedBeats is not installed.

METHOD:: unavailableServices
A service port whose every operation reports the given error, so the window
can explain what is missing.

ARGUMENT:: error
The MBError to report.

METHOD:: clearCurrent
Forget the current window (called when it closes).

EXAMPLES::

code::
MaxxedBeats.gui;
::
